{% set plans = [
    {id: 1, title: 'Monthly box', periodUnit: 'month', periodCount: 1, trialDays: 0, installmentCount: null, commitmentCount: 3, pausable: true, priceUntaxed: 9.9, priceTaxed: 11.88},
    {id: 2, title: 'Quarterly box with trial', periodUnit: 'quarter', periodCount: 1, trialDays: 14, installmentCount: 4, commitmentCount: null, pausable: false, priceUntaxed: 24.9, priceTaxed: 29.88},
] %}
<div class="Story">
<div class="Story-section">
    <h4 class="Story-title">Base (signed-in customer)</h4>
    <p class="Story-label">
        The choice between a one-time purchase and a subscription plan, on the product sheet: period, price of one
        installment as the buyer reads prices, trial, commitment, number of installments and whether the plan can be
        paused. In the product component the radios are bound to its `selectedPlan` model; here they only show the states.
    </p>
    <div class="Story-stage Story-stage--roomy">
        <twig:Organisms:SubscriptionPlanChooser:Base :plans="plans" :selectedPlan="2" :signedIn="true" :display="visitor_tax_display()" />
    </div>
</div>
<div class="Story-section">
    <h4 class="Story-title">Base (visitor not signed in)</h4>
    <p class="Story-label">
        The plans are shown disabled, with an invitation to sign in: the core refuses a subscription to a visitor who
        is not a signed-in customer.
    </p>
    <div class="Story-stage Story-stage--roomy">
        <twig:Organisms:SubscriptionPlanChooser:Base :plans="plans" :selectedPlan="0" :signedIn="false" name="plan_choice_guest" :display="visitor_tax_display()" />
    </div>
</div>
</div>
